   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public service law, in relation to prohibiting telephone,\ncable and utility companies from charging a fee to customers who request\ncopies of previous billing statements or statements verifying that they are a\ncustomer",
    "basePrintNo": "S4194",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4194-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§224-b & 44, Pub Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4194\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public service law, in relation to prohibiting tele-\nphone, cable and utility companies from charging a fee to customers who\nrequest copies of previous billing statements or statements verifying\nthat they are a customer\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo prohibit telephone, cable and utility companies from charging custom-\ners for previous billing statements.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends section 224-b of the public service law.\n\nSection two amends section 44 of the public service law by adding a new\nsubdivision 6. Section three establishes the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCopies of previous billing statements from telephone, cable or utility\ncompanies are often requested as proof of name identification or resi-\ndency at a certain address. These statements may be necessary for\nòcompleting tasks at the Department of Motor Vehicles, Department of\nSocial Services or other government agencies. However, if a customer\nrequests a copy of a previous billing statement, some telephone, cable\nand utility companies unnecessarily impose a fee to comply with such\nrequest. The cost of providing a copy of a statement to a customer is\nnominal, and companies should not charge for simply providing a customer\nwith such documentation.\n\nThis legislation will prohibit telephone, cable and utility companies\nfrom charging customers for copies of previous billing statements or\nstatements verifying that the person is a customer.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
